# diff
# Betaflight / SITL (SITL) 4.5.1
#
# THE DEFAULT TUNE: BETAFLIGHT 4.5.1'S FACTORY TUNE, WITH FOUR SETTINGS
# CHANGED.
#
# Every PID and filter value below is Betaflight 4.5.1's own factory
# default, which is what a freshly flashed 5 inch quad flies before anyone
# touches it, except the four under WHAT IS NOT FACTORY. Since Karate race
# and Precision were removed it is the only tune that ships.
#
# Until 2026-09-28 there were no exceptions, and the reason for that still
# holds for every other line: fly this, change something on the bench, and
# the difference is the thing you changed. The owner made the exceptions
# that day, from the board's feel reports. "Slow to answer the stick" is
# the form's most ticked box, on 23 reports, 11 of them since 24 September,
# every one flown on this tune with no slider moved; "bounces back after a
# stop" was ticked on 9, all on this tune and 8 of them stock. The owner's
# ask: feedforward, a little, on the default tune, and fix the bounce back.
#
# npm run feel:response flies this file beside Betaflight's factory tune on
# every run, with the factory values read out of the module rather than
# typed, and the numbers below are its output unless they say otherwise:
# the five inch at its own 1.62 g, Betaflight's default rates, and pads at
# the rates the reports show.
#
# WHAT IS NOT FACTORY, AND WHY.
#
# 1. Feedforward a quarter up: simplified_feedforward_gain 125, which is
#    f_roll 150, f_pitch 156 and f_yaw 150 (factory 100, and 120, 125 and
#    120). Feedforward pushes on the stick's movement before any error
#    exists, which is what "slow to answer the stick" is about. A fast flick
#    now reaches 90 percent of its rate 3 to 5 ms sooner on every pad the
#    reports show, the rate trails a 2 Hz stick sine by 1.8 to 2.7 ms less,
#    and the overshoot does not move. It is written as the slider and not
#    only as F, because `simplified_tuning apply` computes F as Betaflight's
#    factory F times the sliders: a bare f_roll = 150 would go back to 120
#    the first time a pilot touched the master on the PIDs screen. The F
#    values are the ones that command computes at 125, read back from the
#    module, and the PIDs screen's Stick response slider now starts at 125.
#
# 2. iterm_relax_cutoff 10 (factory 15), and
# 3. iterm_relax RPY_INC (factory RP): the bounce back. Betaflight's I term
#    remembers every degree the craft runs on past a stop and hands it back
#    once the craft has stopped, and that is the bounce. Relax holds I back
#    while the stick is moving. At 15 Hz the hold ends before a full stick
#    flip has finished stopping, so I learns the tail of every stop, and
#    factory leaves yaw out of the hold entirely. Feedforward on its own
#    makes the bounce a little worse, so these two carry item 1 as well.
#    With all four, a whole full stick roll ends 0.38 degrees back where
#    factory's ends 1.20, a pitch flip 0.48 where factory's ends 1.62, three
#    quarter stick 0.60 and 0.55 where factory's end 0.89 and 1.03, and in
#    Arcade, where the plant's turbulence cannot blur it, a full stick flip
#    stops moving in half the time.
#
#    INC, which holds I back only while it would grow and lets it shrink,
#    rather than RPY, which holds it either way, because of the pads. A
#    browser refreshes a radio at 125 to 242 Hz and the shell sends the
#    module 250 frames a second, so the module is handed repeated frames,
#    and Betaflight's feedforward reads the first repeat after a movement as
#    a dropped packet and carries the movement on for one more frame
#    (calculateFeedforward in fc/rc.c). At the end of a stop that is a frame
#    too much braking, and I is what takes it back out. RPY stops I doing
#    that too, and on a 160 to 190 Hz pad its half stick stops came back
#    further than factory's did. INC leaves I free to take it back.
#
#    What that does not reach: on a pad near 180 Hz a half stick roll or
#    pitch stop still ends a tenth to a fifth of a degree further back than
#    factory's, with a sharper flick back, about 50 deg/s at its fastest
#    where factory's is under 40. Fed only the pad's new samples the flick
#    drops under 20 deg/s, so it lives in the shell's input path, not here;
#    PROGRESS.md has the probe. And INC's own cost: after a quick bank and
#    back at 0.3 to 0.6 stick the craft ends 0.3 to 0.9 degrees from where
#    the stick put it, where factory ends within 0.13, though after the same
#    at full stick it ends 1.4 to 1.9 off where factory ends 2.1 to 2.5.
#
# 4. pidsum_limit_yaw 500 (factory 400). The comment at that line has the
#    upstream bug it steps past.
#
#    Yaw is where 3 and 4 meet: yaw inside the relax hold, and a yaw I term
#    the anti windup can reach. Together they take the nose's swing back
#    after a whole yaw turn at half, three quarter and full stick from 2.99,
#    7.79 and 8.15 degrees to 2.26, 4.64 and 7.34; feedforward moves them by
#    less than a tenth. What is left is the plant, not the tune: yaw is the
#    axis with the least authority, a full stick stop from 670 deg/s takes
#    about 140 ms with the motors at their limits, and no relax setting
#    covers a stop that long. Yaw P would take more of it, and the PIDs
#    screen's expert table reaches yaw P, but a tune in simplified mode
#    cannot keep one: the first slider a pilot moves puts yaw back to
#    Betaflight's own. A lower yaw rate on the Rates screen would take more,
#    as the three quarter row, a 390 deg/s turn, shows, and so would
#    iterm_limit 200 at full stick; neither was taken.
#
# What the four leave alone: propwash, where a throttle chop and punch
# reads the same to a hundredth of a deg/s; angle mode, which still levels
# without passing level, 19 to 27 ms sooner; and the flying weights from
# 0.97 to 2.27 g and the micro's 2.03, where the flick is 5 ms quicker and
# a full stick flip comes back a quarter or less of what factory's did.
#
# To fly Betaflight's factory tune exactly, put seven values back on the
# Flight controller screen: simplified_feedforward_gain 100, f_roll 120,
# f_pitch 125, f_yaw 120, iterm_relax RP, iterm_relax_cutoff 15 and
# pidsum_limit_yaw 400.
#
# Provenance: every other value is the one in
# betaflight/firmware-presets presets/4.5/tune/defaults.txt and
# presets/4.5/filters/defaults.txt, which are the official statements of
# what 4.5 defaults are. They are written out in full rather than left
# implicit so this file can be diffed against the vendored firmware.
#
# NO RATES. This file sets no rateprofile at all, and neither does any other
# tune here. Rates belong to the pilot, not to a tune, and they are chosen in
# Settings; the shell appends them to whichever tune is loaded. See
# configs/rates.js. Shipping rates inside a tune is what made the Karate
# preset, which this build no longer ships, impossible to judge: choosing it
# changed the tune and the stick authority in one keypress.
#
# Airframe: the reference 5 inch of STAGE1.md, 6S, 1900 kV, 0.65 kg.
#
# The airframe keys below are STORED, not read. The Stage 1 plant's mass,
# kV, cell count and rotor size are constants in src/native/plant.c and
# changing motor_kv here changes nothing about how the craft flies. They
# are kept so a dump round trips and so the numbers are written down
# beside the tune that assumes them. This block used to claim the plant
# read them.

batch start

board_name SITL

# ---- master ----

set motor_kv = 1900
set motor_poles = 14
set vbat_max_cell_voltage = 420
set vbat_min_cell_voltage = 350
set vbat_warning_cell_voltage = 350
set battery_capacity = 1300
set small_angle = 180

# Filters, 4.5 defaults
set gyro_hardware_lpf = NORMAL
set gyro_lpf1_type = PT1
set gyro_lpf1_static_hz = 250
set gyro_lpf2_type = PT1
set gyro_lpf2_static_hz = 500
set gyro_notch1_hz = 0
set gyro_notch1_cutoff = 0
set gyro_notch2_hz = 0
set gyro_notch2_cutoff = 0
set gyro_lpf1_dyn_min_hz = 250
set gyro_lpf1_dyn_max_hz = 500
set gyro_lpf1_dyn_expo = 5
set simplified_gyro_filter = ON
set simplified_gyro_filter_multiplier = 100

set dyn_notch_count = 3
set dyn_notch_q = 300
set dyn_notch_min_hz = 100
set dyn_notch_max_hz = 600

set yaw_spin_recovery = AUTO
set dshot_idle_value = 550
set mixer_type = LEGACY
set yaw_motors_reversed = OFF

# ---- profile 0 ----
profile 0

set pid_at_min_throttle = ON
set anti_gravity_gain = 80
set anti_gravity_cutoff_hz = 5
set anti_gravity_p_gain = 100
set acc_limit_yaw = 0
set acc_limit = 0

set iterm_rotation = OFF
# Not factory (RP and 15): the header, items 2 and 3.
set iterm_relax = RPY_INC
set iterm_relax_type = SETPOINT
set iterm_relax_cutoff = 10
set iterm_windup = 85
set iterm_limit = 400
set pidsum_limit = 500

# 500, not the factory 400. 400 is 40 percent of the mixer's yaw range, and
# Betaflight's anti windup is driven only by getMotorMixRange against
# iterm_windup, so a yaw axis clipped at 40 percent can never on its own
# reach the 85 percent windup point: the I term keeps integrating for the
# whole time the axis is saturated. Round 23 in PROGRESS.md measured it on a
# full stick yaw step, yaw I pinned at its 400 cap for 225 ms, and found the
# discontinuity between 450 and 480 that betaflight/betaflight issue 13486
# reports, open since March 2024. At 500 the windup point is reachable and
# the anti windup does its job on yaw. On its own, on this weight, that
# takes a full stick yaw stop from 164 ms to 141 and its swing back from
# 8.15 degrees to 7.48; with the rest of this tune beside it, three quarter
# stick, where the I term used to pin as well, goes from 7.79 to 4.64.
#
# Until 2026-09-28 this line flew the bug on purpose, because the file's
# whole job was to be what a freshly flashed quad flies, the parts of that
# which are wrong included. The header says why that changed.
set pidsum_limit_yaw = 500

set throttle_boost = 5
set throttle_boost_cutoff = 15

# The three F values are not factory (120, 125, 120): they are what
# simplified_feedforward_gain 125 below computes. The header, item 1.
set p_roll = 45
set i_roll = 80
set d_roll = 40
set f_roll = 150
set p_pitch = 47
set i_pitch = 84
set d_pitch = 46
set f_pitch = 156
set p_yaw = 45
set i_yaw = 80
set d_yaw = 0
set f_yaw = 150

set d_min_roll = 30
set d_min_pitch = 34
set d_min_yaw = 0
set d_max_gain = 37
set d_max_advance = 20

set abs_control_gain = 0
set use_integrated_yaw = OFF

set thrust_linear = 0
set transient_throttle_limit = 0
set feedforward_transition = 0
set feedforward_max_rate_limit = 90

set dyn_idle_min_rpm = 0

set simplified_pids_mode = RPY
set simplified_master_multiplier = 100
set simplified_i_gain = 100
set simplified_d_gain = 100
set simplified_pi_gain = 100
set simplified_dmax_gain = 100
# Not factory (100): the header, item 1.
set simplified_feedforward_gain = 125
set simplified_pitch_d_gain = 100
set simplified_pitch_pi_gain = 100

set tpa_mode = D
set tpa_rate = 65
set tpa_breakpoint = 1350
set tpa_low_rate = 20
set tpa_low_breakpoint = 1050
set tpa_low_always = OFF

set dterm_lpf1_dyn_min_hz = 75
set dterm_lpf1_dyn_max_hz = 150
set dterm_lpf1_dyn_expo = 5
set dterm_lpf1_type = PT1
set dterm_lpf1_static_hz = 75
set dterm_lpf2_type = PT1
set dterm_lpf2_static_hz = 150
set dterm_notch_hz = 0
set dterm_notch_cutoff = 0
set yaw_lowpass_hz = 100
set simplified_dterm_filter = ON
set simplified_dterm_filter_multiplier = 100

batch end
